title **4. Test Full Workflow — Synchronous (No Queue)**

actor Client
participant "RunController" as RC
participant "TestFullWorkflow\nUseCase" as UC
database "Repos\n(Run/Task/Workflow)" as RR
participant "StageRecorder" as SR
participant "EventPublisher" as EP
participant "OrchestrationEngine" as OE
participant "NodeHandler" as NH
participant "WorkerExecutor\n(External)" as WE

note over UC : No orchestration queue\nFully **synchronous** execution

Client -> RC : POST /workflows/{id}/test-full\n{input_data}
activate RC
RC -> UC : execute(TestFullWorkflowCommand)
activate UC

UC -> RR : load workflow, validate DAG
UC -> RR : get/create persistent test_run\n(test_mode="full", is_test=true)
UC -> RR : clear stale state: completed_nodes,\nvariables, cancel old tasks
UC -> RR : run.status = RUNNING, save(run)
UC -> SR : record("run.started")
UC -> EP : publish(**RunStarted**)

UC -> OE : **handle_entry_nodes()** [BLOCKING]
activate OE #FFE0B2

loop process all reachable nodes
  OE -> NH : handle(node)
  NH --> OE : result

  OE -> OE : enqueue ExecuteNodeAction → _exec_uniform()\n(recursive for BUILTINs)
  OE -[#999999]> WE : dispatch TASK nodes
end

note right of OE #FFE0B2 : **Blocks** until all control-flow\nnodes processed or PENDING hit

OE --> UC : return
deactivate OE

UC -> OE : check_run_completion()
UC --> RC : {status, output_data, completed_at}
deactivate UC
RC --> Client : **200 OK** (after full processing)
deactivate RC

note over Client : Response may take **seconds**\nIncludes final result

@enduml

